WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.336
[music playing]

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:14.080
- It's just a really tight-knit
ocean-loving community.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:20.587
Everybody generally has the same
sort of healthy ocean lifestyle

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:23.089
vibe.

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:26.760
That's what makes
this area so unique.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:31.865
- Scott Bass has called San
Diego home for over 40 years.

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:33.099
- I love living here.

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:35.602
You're so close to
what really amounts

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:38.405
to the largest national
park that we have,

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:42.242
which is the Pacific Ocean.

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:45.512
It provides a lot
of fulfillment.

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:54.687
- San Diego is a coastal oasis
for its beautiful shoreline

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:55.755
and marine wildlife.

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:03.196
Just below the surface is a
coastal view of iconic animals,

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:06.466
like the California sea
lion and the official state

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:11.371
marine fish, the
hard-to-miss Garibaldi.

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:15.408
But sitting atop the
food chain are sharks.

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:22.916
Historically, interactions
between sharks and humans

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.284
are rare.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.887
But in 2008, a horrifying
incident occurs.

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:38.765
- There was a lot of disbelief.

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:43.269
This hadn't happened in
San Diego in over 50 years.

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:44.471
It was a sad day.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.178
It felt like summertime.

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:55.515
It was a beautiful
San Diego day.

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:57.383
- In the early
morning, Scott Bass

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:01.120
was paddleboarding along
Fletcher Cove, about 15 miles

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:03.690
north of the city of San Diego.

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:06.493
He's near a group of
triathletes in training.

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:10.630
Among them is retired
veterinarian Dr. Dave Martin.

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:14.734
- Dr. Martin was swimming
with his triathlete group.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:19.439
They were approximately 150
yards off of the surf line.

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:24.677
- But somewhere below the
group, a predator takes aim.

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:29.516
[loud bang]

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:34.120
A shark sinks its teeth
into Dr. Martin's legs

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:37.657
and launches him
out of the water.

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:39.692
He screams for help.

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:41.461
- Help!

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:45.632
- Everyone in the
water is stunned.

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:46.633
- It was very surreal.

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:52.272
People were scared.

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:54.807
- Dr. Martin
disappears underwater.

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:07.754
Finally, the shark
releases its hold,

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:12.225
and the group pulls Dr.
Martin back to shore.

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:14.961
First responders
race into action.

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:16.362
[helicopter rotor blades]

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:18.631
- I remember the helicopter
came right above me

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:22.669
and just boomed down on me,
"There's been a shark attack.

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:26.105
Please get out of the
water immediately."

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:29.909
- But for Dr. Martin,
the injuries to his legs

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.578
are too severe.

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:35.014
Before he can be
transported to a hospital,

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:36.649
he succumbs to his injuries.

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:42.889
The tragedy captures the
attention of Southern

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:44.591
California residents.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:46.125
- There was a lot
of police there.

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:47.360
There was a lot of media there.

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:48.494
There was a lot of shock.

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:50.730
There was a lot of sadness.

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:52.398
There was a lot of despair.

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:56.235
- And news outlets
cover it worldwide.

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:57.570
- You know, it's a big deal.

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:59.372
You know, there hasn't
been a shark attack--

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:01.941
a fatal shark attack in
San Diego in something

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:04.711
like 50 years.

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:07.246
- Residents are stunned.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:11.217
Since 1970, the area has
averaged about one attack

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:13.419
every three years.

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:16.723
But Dr. Martin's
fatal incident in 2008

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:20.593
is just the harbinger
of things to come.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:25.098
In 2009, a sudden
spike takes hold, six

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:27.634
attacks in only seven months.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:31.070
- I'm sure any number of
parents were concerned.

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:33.940
People were trying
to figure it out.

00:04:34.007 --> 00:04:36.576
[music playing]

